<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>UiPath.UIAutomation.Activities</id>
    <version>18.4.5</version>
    <title>UiPath.UIAutomation.Activities</title>
    <authors>UiPath</authors>
    <owners>UiPath</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>true</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <licenseUrl>https://www.uipath.com/hubfs/legalspot/UiPath_EULA.pdf</licenseUrl>
    <projectUrl>https://activities.uipath.com/docs/about-the-ui-automation-activities-pack</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>http://www.uipath.com/favicon.ico</iconUrl>
    <description>IMPORTANT: Installing this package on a Studio v2018.2 or lower causes unexpected changes in your workflows. This package version requires Studio v2018.3 or above.
Core activities which enable the robots to simulate human interaction such as mouse, keystrokes and image recognition. Package also contains activities for event monitoring, image, browser and window manipulation.</description>
    <releaseNotes>The UIAutomation package has been upgraded to address some issues regarding data scraping on Java applications v1.3 to 1.6, and the installation of the Chrome extension.

Bug Fixes
* The *Extract Structured Data* activity did not return any data when used with Java applications v1.3 to v1.6.
* When selecting web page elements in Internet Explorer, the wrong `idx`attribute would be generated, causing selectors to become invalid.
* The Chrome extension would fail to install after upgrading Google Chrome to version 73.

For the full Release Notes, please visit https://activities.uipath.com/docs/release-notes-ui-automation.</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="AvalonEdit" version="5.0.3" />
      <dependency id="Caliburn.Micro" version="3.0.1" />
      <dependency id="Extended.Wpf.Toolkit" version="2.8.0" />
      <dependency id="Humanizer.Core" version="2.4.2" />
      <dependency id="UiPath.Vision" version="1.2.0" />
      <dependency id="UiPath" version="10.0.7020.22745" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
</package>